## Spec workflow

<!-- Delete this section if the workspace does not use spec-driven development. For an sdd
     workspace do not hand-write it: `/sdd init` adds the `<!-- sdd:begin -->` block. -->

- Requirements live in **Azure DevOps** ({org}/{project}) and are mirrored read-only into
  `{specRoot}/**/<ado-id>-<slug>/requirements.md` by `/sdd sync`. Never edit a mirrored
  requirement: fix the work item and re-sync, or the fix is silently overwritten.
- `design.md`, `tasks.md` and `questions.md` in the same folder are repo-owned and never pushed to ADO.
- The spec folder tree mirrors the ADO hierarchy; resolve a folder by glob `{specRoot}/**/<id>-*/`,
  never by remembered path.
- `ado_id` is the join key between work item, spec folder, branch and PR.
- Use `/sdd` for anything spec-related (`/sdd:sdd` for help).

